│  adhering to the Treasurer's single-table mandate. \n\n*   **Logic:** By     │
│  placing the \"buffers\" (David, Fiona, and Charlie) between the most        │
│  volatile parties, we prevent direct conflict while keeping the group        │
│  integrated.\n\n| Position | Guest | Note |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n|       │
│  **Seat 1** | **Eve** | Furthest from Bob (End of table). |\n| **Seat 2** |  │
│  **Fiona** | Serves as a buffer between Eve and Alice. |\n| **Seat 3** |     │
│  **Alice** | Away from Charlie; near Fiona. |\n| **Seat 4** | **David** |    │
│  Buffer between Alice and Bob. |\n| **Seat 5** | **Bob** | Seated away from  │
│  Eve; near David. |\n| **Seat 6** | **Charlie** | Seated at the opposite     │
│  end of the table from Alice. |\n\n---\n\n### **3. Final Logistics & Safety  │
│  Summary**\n*   **Dietary Integrity:** While the menu has been               │
│  consolidated, the strict gluten-free preparation protocols remain for all   │
│  guests to ensure Charlie’s safety. The transition to a two-tier menu        │
│  allows for higher quality ingredients within the $500 budget.\n*            │
│  **Conflict Resolution:** \n    *   **Alice** is no longer near Charlie. \n  │
│  *   **Eve** is separated from **Bob** by the entire length of the table     │
│  and three intervening guests.\n    *   **Bob and David** remain close,      │
│  preserving their social requirement.\n    *   **Fiona** remains near        │
│  **Alice** as requested.\n    *   **Charlie** is placed at the opposite end  │
│  of the table from **Alice** to satisfy her negative constraint. \n\nThis    │
│  plan represents the only path to a fiscally solvent and logistically        │
│  functional event. All guests are expected to remain in their assigned       │
│  seats to ensure the evening proceeds without further                        │
│  incident.","negotiation_summary":"The negotiation process was               │
│  characterized by intense interpersonal conflicts and a major intervention   │
│  from the Treasurer. Guests initially demanded highly specific, conflicting  │
│  seating arrangements—particularly regarding Alice and Charlie’s mutual      │
│  antipathy and Eve’s refusal to sit near carnivores like Bob. As the Host    │
│  attempted to resolve these social puzzles, the Treasurer intervened to      │
│  shut down the logistical complexity, mandating a consolidated menu and a    │
│  single rectangular table to stay under a strict $500 budget.\n\nIn the      │
│  final iteration, the Host successfully satisfied the Treasurer by merging   │
│  the menus into two tiers and placing everyone at one table. While most      │
│  social buffers were maintained to keep the peace, total consensus was       │
│  impossible because some guests, like Charlie, had their specific social     │
│  preferences overridden to satisfy the Host's priority of enforcing Alice's  │
│  negative constraints."}                                                     │
