│                                                                              │
│  Agent: Head Caterer                                                         │
│                                                                              │
│  Final Answer:                                                               │
│  As the Head Caterer, I have carefully reviewed the conflicting dietary      │
│  requirements of your guests. Given the extreme divergence between the       │
│  Carnivore diet (Bob) and the Vegan/Vegetarian diets (Alice, Eve), a single  │
│  communal meal is not feasible.                                              │
│                                                                              │
│  To ensure safety and full compliance with all guests' dietary needs, I      │
│  have designed a **Universal Component Menu**. This allows every guest to    │
│  enjoy a cohesive dining experience while adhering to their specific         │
│  restrictions by utilizing modular, high-quality ingredients prepared in     │
│  segregated stations to prevent cross-contamination.                         │
│                                                                              │
│  ### The Inclusive Menu                                                      │
│                                                                              │
│  **Appetizer: The Harvest & Protein Board**                                  │
│  *   **For Alice, Charlie, Fiona, and David:** A selection of roasted root   │
│  vegetables, herbed quinoa, and artisanal gluten-free crackers.              │
│  *   **For Bob:** A curated selection of premium sliced grass-fed beef       │
│  carpaccio and cured venison (No plant-based additives).                     │
│  *   **For Eve:** A selection of roasted root vegetables, herbed quinoa,     │
│  and artisanal gluten-free crackers (Certified Vegan).                       │
│                                                                              │
│  **Entrée: Build-Your-Own Culinary Experience**                              │
│  *   **The Protein Station:**                                                │
│      *   *Vegan/Vegetarian:* Grilled cauliflower steaks with a balsamic      │
│  reduction.                                                                  │
│      *   *Pescatarian:* Pan-seared wild-caught salmon with lemon and herbs.  │
│      *   *Carnivore:* Prime ribeye steak, seared in pure tallow (No          │
│  seasonings containing plant extracts).                                      │
│  *   **The Accompaniment Station:**                                          │
│      *   *Gluten-Free Base:* A starch-heavy medley of roasted potatoes and   │
│  wild rice.                                                                  │
│      *   *Vegan Side:* Steamed seasonal greens (garlic/oil only).            │
│      *   *Note:* The sauce for the vegans/vegetarians will be a honey-free,  │
│  plant-based reduction; the sauce for the meat eaters will be a              │
│  pan-reduction using natural meat juices.                                    │
│                                                                              │
│  **Dessert: The Deconstructed Trio**                                         │
│  *   **For Alice, Charlie, Fiona, and David:** A rich, flourless dark        │
│  chocolate torte (contains dairy/eggs).                                      │
│  *   **For Eve:** A fresh berry compote with coconut-cream reduction         │
